WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.110 --> 00:00:04.150
- You guys probably know that
I have a pup Husky named Roxy,

00:00:04.150 --> 00:00:06.910
and while I thought that
it's cool to own a dog,

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:10.000
I think it'd be so much
cooler to own a bear.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.913
Meet Bear Varshavski.

00:00:12.986 --> 00:00:14.841
♪ Bippity-bop and hippity-hop ♪

00:00:14.841 --> 00:00:17.842
♪ I'm as happy as I can be ♪

00:00:17.842 --> 00:00:20.613
♪ I'm gonna dum, dum,
dum, and zippity zoom ♪

00:00:20.613 --> 00:00:24.234
♪ Love is sweet, love is
grand, it works wonderfully ♪

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.479
♪ Woooh, we bop and zippity-hop ♪

00:00:26.479 --> 00:00:29.241
♪ I'm as happy as I can be ♪

00:00:29.241 --> 00:00:31.865
♪ I'm gonna dum, dum,
dum, and zippity zoom ♪

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:36.865
♪ I'm in love, I'm in love,
I'm in love, I don't care ♪

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:40.653
Come on, come on little boy.

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:44.720
Come here, come on daddy's lap.

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:48.320
Yes this is little Bear
Varshavski my new pup.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:51.240
And I know your first
reaction, what about Roxy?

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.810
Don't worry Roxy's not going anywhere,

00:00:52.810 --> 00:00:54.800
she's my little pup forever and ever.

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:58.090
Like most of you know, I
do share Roxy with my dad.

00:00:58.090 --> 00:01:00.600
In fact, we got Roxy together when my mom

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:03.320
passed away to have
something to bond over.

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.900
But now a days since I'm
living apart from my dad,

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.720
I feel awful when I have
to take Roxy away from him

00:01:08.720 --> 00:01:11.390
and then leave him alone
'cause it makes him really sad

00:01:11.390 --> 00:01:14.330
and on the other hand, when I
have to give Roxy back to him

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:16.850
I get really sad 'cause want
to still have a pup around.

00:01:16.850 --> 00:01:20.170
What better way to
celebrate being a dog lover,

00:01:20.170 --> 00:01:22.930
get health benefits, cheer up myself,

00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:26.340
cheer up my dad, and get
Roxy an awesome brother

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.230
then to get a little
Newfie and name him Bear.

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:31.780
A Newfie is a Newfoundland, and I know

00:01:31.780 --> 00:01:33.760
it sounds like I'm saying New-fin-land

00:01:33.760 --> 00:01:36.590
but I'm saying New-found-land in a way

00:01:36.590 --> 00:01:37.990
that it's properly pronounced,

00:01:37.990 --> 00:01:39.360
so I'm still learning myself.

00:01:39.360 --> 00:01:42.410
This little guy here, right
now he's only eight weeks old

00:01:42.410 --> 00:01:47.200
he's technically tiny but he
weighs basically half of Roxy.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:48.650
So you can imagine, he's gonna be

00:01:48.650 --> 00:01:52.530
probably 150 pounds when
he grows up full size.

00:01:52.530 --> 00:01:54.530
He's gonna be a huge beast.

00:01:54.530 --> 00:01:56.360
The highlight of the Newfoundland breed

00:01:56.360 --> 00:01:58.100
is their temperament.

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:00.110
These guys are known as gentle giants

00:02:00.110 --> 00:02:01.740
for a very good reason.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:05.440
They're amazing with kids,
they're amazing with people,

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.160
they're basically giant people pleasers.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.790
And that's how their breed came to be,

00:02:09.790 --> 00:02:13.110
they were working dogs
that helped haul loads,

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:15.440
they helped rescue
people that were drowning

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:16.980
'cause they're excellent swimmers

00:02:16.980 --> 00:02:19.450
because of these webbed
huge feet of theirs.

00:02:19.450 --> 00:02:22.780
I mean, his paw is bigger than my wrist.

00:02:22.780 --> 00:02:25.982
I don't have the biggest
wrists in the world, but Jesus.

00:02:25.982 --> 00:02:26.950
(dog hiccups)

00:02:26.950 --> 00:02:28.053
He has hiccups.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.010
Growing pups always have hiccups,

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.410
that's not new, so that
doesn't even concern me.

00:02:35.894 --> 00:02:36.727
(laughs)

00:02:36.727 --> 00:02:37.640
I'm sure you've heard that there are

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:39.470
health benefits to owning a pup,

00:02:39.470 --> 00:02:42.100
but do you know exactly what
all those health benefits are?

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.700
Anxiety and depression.

00:02:43.700 --> 00:02:46.010
We know that dogs make us feel good,

00:02:46.010 --> 00:02:49.820
but actually they're great at
warding off mental illness.

00:02:49.820 --> 00:02:52.680
Yes, those who have pups, generally have

00:02:52.680 --> 00:02:55.100
less anxiety and less depressive symptoms.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.680
We don't have a clear
understanding of why dogs

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.660
help with anxiety and depression,

00:02:59.660 --> 00:03:02.550
but we know that they
definitely make you more social.

00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.540
And this is great for all ages.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:05.870
Kids benefit from this.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:08.550
There was a study talking about how kids

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.740
who are autistic benefited greatly

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:13.610
by spending time with a dog,
it's great for socialization.

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:16.420
Another point in life it's really good for

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:18.470
is when your 20s and your 30s

00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:19.990
and you're trying to find someone new

00:03:19.990 --> 00:03:22.130
and your dating and it's not that easy.

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:22.963
Guess what?

00:03:22.963 --> 00:03:25.430
Get an adorable pup, go to the dog park,

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.450
meet some dog people, 'cause generally

00:03:27.450 --> 00:03:29.450
dog people are really awesome people.

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:31.000
I don't know why I did awesome people.

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:32.590
We've talked about the negative effects

00:03:32.590 --> 00:03:34.240
of chronic stress on your body

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:37.970
and a lot of that is the result
of the chronic activation

00:03:37.970 --> 00:03:39.420
of your sympathetic nervous system.

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:41.500
That's that flight or fight response

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:43.100
that keeps you always on edge.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.400
Well guess what, having a dog,

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:48.180
petting a dog, lowers your blood pressure,

00:03:48.180 --> 00:03:50.370
calms your sympathetic nervous system.

00:03:50.370 --> 00:03:52.860
You get a lot of health
benefits from that.

00:03:52.860 --> 00:03:54.810
Not only is your heart healthy

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.550
'cause your blood pressure is lower,

00:03:56.550 --> 00:03:59.430
but in studies when we've
looked at dog owners

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:01.440
and comparing them to non-dog owners,

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.720
we've found that the dog owners had

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:05.110
lower cholesterol, lower triglycerides,

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:07.900
and that really makes a
difference for heart health.

00:04:07.900 --> 00:04:10.270
It reduces the risks of
heart attack, strokes.

00:04:10.270 --> 00:04:12.470
If you can reduce the chance
of having one of these

00:04:12.470 --> 00:04:15.010
major illnesses and
diseases happen to you,

00:04:15.010 --> 00:04:17.090
just by owning an amazing dog.

00:04:17.090 --> 00:04:19.600
Well this is not directly
a health benefit,

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.840
I think this is incredibly awesome.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.390
Dogs' noses are 40 times more sensitive

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.860
than a human's nose is.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:28.230
And what dogs have been able to do

00:04:28.230 --> 00:04:30.950
is sniff and detect cancer.

00:04:30.950 --> 00:04:32.410
Initially, this was just based

00:04:32.410 --> 00:04:35.070
on anecdotal evidence,
people telling stories

00:04:35.070 --> 00:04:37.190
that a dog was licking their lump

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:38.150
and they got it checked out

00:04:38.150 --> 00:04:39.710
and found out that it was cancer,

00:04:39.710 --> 00:04:42.480
but now we have scientific
research on this

00:04:42.480 --> 00:04:43.860
to the point where we're thinking

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:47.160
about using dogs in medical care for this.

00:04:47.160 --> 00:04:49.550
It's incredible, dogs can smell cancer.

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:52.400
Contrary to popular belief, having a dog

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.750
in a household actually
decreases the likelihood

00:04:55.750 --> 00:04:57.800
that your children will develop asthma,

00:04:57.800 --> 00:05:00.950
eczema, or allergies, and that's usually

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:03.290
a trio that runs in tandem together.

00:05:03.290 --> 00:05:05.420
Let's get out of science
land for a moment.

00:05:05.420 --> 00:05:07.880
Not only do you see benefits within

00:05:07.880 --> 00:05:10.200
heart attack patients, depressed patients,

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:12.590
Alzheimer's patients,
but the biggest benefit

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:16.000
and the most exciting stuff
that I've seen research on,

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:18.220
is that they compared people who own dogs

00:05:18.220 --> 00:05:20.810
and people who don't
own dogs and guess what?

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:23.500
Those who own a dog, drastically

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.410
and significantly extend their lives.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.130
And we don't have a clear
explanation for that,

00:05:28.130 --> 00:05:30.550
whether that means dog
owners take more walks

00:05:30.550 --> 00:05:33.630
and are more active, is it
because they're more social,

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:36.820
is it because their stress
levels are lower 'cause they're

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:39.430
constantly petting and
playing with their dogs?

00:05:39.430 --> 00:05:41.830
It's likely a combination
of all of these factors.

00:05:41.830 --> 00:05:44.590
What's cool about having a big dog is that

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:48.280
they can serve as guide
dogs, as rescue dogs,

00:05:48.280 --> 00:05:50.410
they're so smart,
they're very intelligent,

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:52.680
they're people friendly,
and that combination

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:55.470
is really good for a working dog to have.

00:05:55.470 --> 00:05:57.470
Now, I don't think I'm going to be doing

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:59.680
a lot of rescue missions here with Bear,

00:05:59.680 --> 00:06:01.260
but what I will be doing is I'm gonna

00:06:01.260 --> 00:06:03.300
get him certified as a therapy dog,

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.070
and days that I can, I'm gonna bring him

00:06:05.070 --> 00:06:07.890
into the hospital for my
patients to play with him.

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:10.910
Because he's so calm, he's so friendly,

00:06:10.910 --> 00:06:12.870
and a lot of times in the hospital

00:06:12.870 --> 00:06:15.760
where patients are sick,
we tend to be afraid

00:06:15.760 --> 00:06:18.230
to bring humor and
happiness into the situation

00:06:18.230 --> 00:06:20.650
because we feel like it
might upset the patients.

00:06:20.650 --> 00:06:22.700
But in reality, patients need a laugh,

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.940
they need a good time, those who are sick

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:26.470
need a laugh the most.

00:06:26.470 --> 00:06:29.170
So I hope that Bear can
be an awesome therapy dog,

00:06:29.170 --> 00:06:31.080
we can bring him into the hospital,

00:06:31.080 --> 00:06:33.800
maybe we can bring him on
a curbside consult with us

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:37.420
and ask people questions on
the street with Bear with us.

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:40.310
I hope that you guys
enjoy him as much as I do,

00:06:40.310 --> 00:06:42.590
there's gonna be tons of
pictures of him on Instagram

00:06:42.590 --> 00:06:45.571
and all over social media,
so please like those.

